    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8635ffdb6f2a40e4bd581a66175b6c13",
      "statement": "GitHub App installation tokens expire after about an hour, so agent/github/proxy.py records each thread's token expiry and scope and maybe_refresh_proxy_token re-mints and re-applies the token when within PROXY_TOKEN_REFRESH_WINDOW (5 minutes) of expiry or after PROXY_TOKEN_FALLBACK_TTL (50 minutes) when expiry is unknown, preserving the original repository and permission scope so rotation never broadens the token.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/github/proxy.py#L1-L37",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c77892d6582550c9a4d37b07cfb59319da283b45528c6332f60244f037e95fbf:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/github/proxy.py#L112-L189",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fb7bea3fc7cef97da0b06318e20a54d9265e92218675be846ee2492bf73294d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0360f8d8a7e446aa92850cd110db81d7",
      "statement": "The local provider runs a LocalShellBackend directly on the host with no isolation, scoping git config --global to a sandbox-local .gitconfig-sandbox (that includes the developer's real ~/.gitconfig) so the per-run bot identity does not clobber the host identity, and excluding model/provider API keys from the inherited environment.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/sandboxes/providers/local.py#L1-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8b640be9d9f9c5efed4484982a7f6e662a38a18a58d3e236af31ed760535c48c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_899a3784753c4c428bf857c7873906fe",
      "statement": "validate_sandbox_startup_config runs the active provider's configuration validation at server startup so config errors surface at boot rather than on first sandbox creation; for langsmith it delegates to LangSmithProvider.validate_startup_config, which only warns (non-fatally) when DEFAULT_SANDBOX_SNAPSHOT_ID is unset and validates the numeric DEFAULT_SANDBOX_* variables parse as integers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/sandboxes/providers/registry.py#L97-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87c51d7612345fac7461e929312b5fb3c6f4b4fc4b9a690c6b08a4df32ef327b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8bfd833b2aee4551907ca057550352d3",
      "statement": "For the cached and reconnect cases there is no separate reachability ping: _connect_existing_sandbox relies on the GitHub proxy refresh, which must reach the box anyway and raises SandboxUnreachableError when it cannot.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/sandboxes/lifecycle.py#L246-L287",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:11f8a3b600778556ca4f04fb5c4ba6c719f25c866cbe93ef947faec696db36d1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c534f581e9ab478b949d7cf0755db44c",
      "statement": "SandboxGoneError signals a sandbox that no longer exists; because a deleted box holds no working tree and the stale metadata id is what every later run reconnects to, ensure_sandbox_for_thread always replaces it to avoid bricking the thread permanently.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://agent/sandboxes/lifecycle.py#L372-L403",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8518b00bcfaee1fd81215a7635312049e51e621b985cc38f386827bfb7ea49f8:"
